      "payload": {
        "jobId": "be5cc1fa-c765-43f1-9b86-f2f1cf608dd8",
        "draftId": "artifact-output-1-linkedin_post",
        "platform": "linkedin_post",
        "text": "Describe Done Before You Call It Done\n\nYour product isn't done when it looks good to you.\n\nIt's done when you can describe what finished looks like.\n\nThat's the mistake a lot of builders make. You're staring at your own work and it looks so good — but to someone else, it doesn't make sense yet.\n\nSharing it early isn't about asking them to validate your idea.\n\nIt's about letting them have an opinion on what you're building so you can improve it.\n\nBefore you call it done, answer these 3:\n\n1. WHO are you building it for?\n2. WHAT job does it do for them?\n3. WHAT does the finished product look like — even if it's not built yet?\n\nNot a vague scope idea. A complete, done thing you can already describe and use.\n\nIf you can't answer all three correctly, you're not ready to ship.\n\nWhich one is blurriest for you right now — 1, 2, or 3?",
        "valid": true
      }
    },
